---
import LegalLayout from "@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro";

const title = "Terms";
const description =
  "The terms that will govern ListBulkly: what the tool does, what it deliberately does not do, and who owns the artwork and listings you create.";
---

<LegalLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <p>
    <strong>Draft.</strong> These terms describe the product as it is built. The
    contact address is real; the legal entity and jurisdiction are still
    PLACEHOLDER and must be completed before launch. This draft is not yet a
    binding agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>What ListBulkly is</h2>
  <p>
    ListBulkly is a local-first workspace for print-on-demand sellers. It helps you
    prepare artwork, map a Printify print area onto mockup photos, compose listing
    images, write listing copy and send drafts to Printify. Your library is stored in
    your own browser, not on our servers.
  </p>

  <h2>What it deliberately does not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>It does not publish anything by itself. <strong>Publish is a separate, explicit action.</strong></li>
    <li>It does not create products anywhere except the Printify account you connect.</li>
    <li>It does not guarantee sales, ranking, search volume or revenue, and it does not invent those numbers.</li>
    <li>It does not submit Etsy listings. Etsy research is read-only.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your account, your keys, your responsibility</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Keys you paste in Settings are stored in your browser and used for the requests you trigger. Keep your device and browser secure.</li>
    <li>You are responsible for complying with Printify's, Etsy's and any AI provider's terms, including their limits and fees.</li>
    <li>You are responsible for the artwork, text and tags you upload, and for having the rights to sell them.</li>
    <li>You are responsible for the prices, taxes and shipping you send to Printify.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You agree not to use ListBulkly to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>upload or sell content that infringes someone else's intellectual property, privacy or other rights;</li>
    <li>create listings for illegal, deceptive or prohibited products;</li>
    <li>attempt to break, overload or reverse the service's access controls, or use it to attack a third-party service;</li>
    <li>share a single account or key in a way that breaches a provider's terms.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Beta and prototype features</h2>
  <p>
    The companion browser extension is a beta prototype. It is installed unpacked and
    is not yet published to a store. It can change or be withdrawn. The clipboard and
    bookmarklet path remains the documented fallback.
  </p>

  <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
  <p>
    The service is provided as-is while it is being prepared for launch. Features may
    change, and an integration may stop working when a provider changes its API. When
    that happens the app reports the provider's message rather than pretending the
    action succeeded.
  </p>

  <h2>Fees</h2>
  <p>
    Pricing is <strong>PLACEHOLDER</strong>. No payment is taken today, and no plan is
    sold. When billing is switched on, the price, billing period, cancellation and
    refund terms will be published before the first charge. See
    <a href="/refunds">Refunds</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Your content, your ownership</h2>
  <p>
    You keep ownership of your artwork and the copy you write. You grant us only the
    limited permission needed to relay a request you trigger to a provider. Because
    the library lives in your browser, we do not hold a copy that could be sold or
    reused.
  </p>

  <h2>Disclaimer and limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    ListBulkly does not warrant that a listing will be accepted by Printify or Etsy,
    that a product will print as expected, or that the service will be uninterrupted.
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, and once the operating entity is confirmed
    (<strong>PLACEHOLDER — governing law and jurisdiction</strong>), liability is
    limited to the amount you paid for the service in the preceding twelve months.
    Nothing here excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded.
  </p>

  <h2>Ending use</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop using the service at any time and clear your browser data. When
    accounts exist, you will be able to delete the account; until then there is no
    account to delete for the local tools.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:listbulkly@gmail.com">listbulkly@gmail.com</a>.
    The full contact details are on the <a href="/contact">Contact</a> page.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
